So like I said, I'm Fennel, and as you can
see, I'm a scientist.{VAR BE01}
In fact, the subject I'm researching
is Trainers!{VAR BE01}
Professor Juniper is my friend
from college.{VAR BE01}
She asked me to help you guys.{VAR BE01}

So!{VAR BE01}
I'll give you something to help you.
This is a Hidden Machine for you!{VAR BE01}

There are some moves that a Pokémon can
use even when it is not fighting!{VAR BE01}
With this Hidden Machine, you can teach
your Pokémon a move called Cut.{VAR BE00}
It can cut down a small tree.{VAR BE01}
And you can use the Hidden Machine as
many times as you want, like a TM.{VAR BE00}
Isn't that great?{VAR BE01}
But it's difficult to make a Pokémon
forget a hidden move once it learns it.{VAR BE01}

And I'd like to ask you a favor, too!{VAR BE01}
There is a place called the Dreamyard
on the outskirts of Striaton City.{VAR BE01}
I'd like some of the Dream Mist that a
Pokémon there called Munna gives off.{VAR BE01}
With that, I'll be able to use
{VAR FF00 0002}Game Sync {VAR FF00 0000}to collect save files of{VAR BE00}
various Trainers!

Fennel: Did Juniper ask you to complete
the Pokédex?{VAR BE01}
It is a challenge to update the Pokédex
regularly, isn't it?{VAR BE01}
Oops! I got distracted! Please bring me
some of the Dream Mist that Munna{VAR BE00}
gives off in the Dreamyard!

Fennel: Ta-da!{VAR BE01}
Thanks to you, I got some Dream Mist,
and now I can collect save files of{VAR BE00}
various Trainers!{VAR BE00}
Thank you very much!{VAR BE01}
As a token of my appreciation,
I will give you this C-Gear to use!{VAR BE01}
The C-Gear is a device related to
communications, such as{VAR BE00}
Infrared Connection or{VAR BE00}
Nintendo Wi-Fi Connection.{VAR BE01}

Wireless communications
are turned OFF.{VAR BE01}
Turn wireless communications
ON in the System Settings.{VAR BE00}
Error code: 50699{VAR BE01}

You see! The C-Gear was activated, and
that screen showed up!{VAR BE01}
If you touch the “?" icon at the
bottom-right of the screen, you can read{VAR BE00}
about the C-Gear.{VAR BE01}

If you want to turn on the C-Gear, touch
the Power symbol at the bottom right of{VAR BE00}
the screen.{VAR BE01}
Then, after turning on the power, if you
touch the “?" icon at the bottom right{VAR BE00}
of the screen, you can read about{VAR BE00}
the C-Gear.{VAR BE01}

About {VAR FF00 0002}Game Sync{VAR FF00 0000}...{VAR BE01}
I'd like to explain a little more about the
system to collect Trainers' save files.{VAR BE01}
Do you have time to learn more?

I am sorry!
I am so happy, so I will explain about it!{VAR BE01}
Because, thanks to you, we can do a
great thing!{VAR BE01}

Now {VAR FF00 0002}Game Sync {VAR FF00 0000}can retrieve memories
of sleeping Pokémon using Dream Mist!{VAR BE01}
That's right! We can collect save files of
Trainers from all over the world!{VAR BE01}

What's more, we learned that if you use
{VAR FF00 0002}Game Sync{VAR FF00 0000} to make a Pokémon sleep,{VAR BE00}
it will have dreams.{VAR BE01}
Then, when you wake up that Pokémon,
its dream becomes the reality in a{VAR BE00}
space called {VAR FF00 0001}Entralink {VAR FF00 0000}in the middle of{VAR BE00}
the Unova region.{VAR BE01}
Isn't Game Sync interesting?
If you like, please send your save file.{VAR BE01}
I've summed up the details in the PC, so
please check it if you get a chance!{VAR BE01}

Fennel: {VAR FF00 0002}Game Sync{VAR FF00 0000} is fascinating, I think.
Do you think so, too?{VAR BE01}
If you get interested, please send your
save file.{VAR BE01}
I've summed up the details in the PC
at the back.{VAR BE00}
So, please check it, if you'd like!

Fennel: Oh, thank you! {VAR BE01}
You also sent your save file. I saw it
while I was researching Trainers!{VAR BE01}
Isn't {VAR FF00 0002}Game Sync{VAR FF00 0000} great?

Are you a Trainer?{VAR BE01}
Do you use the PC at Pokémon Centers?{VAR BE01}
I am Amanita. I maintain the Box system.
Do you know about the Battle Box?

Amanita: Impressive!{VAR BE01}
If there's a Pokémon you often use in
your battles, you can register it in the{VAR BE00}
Battle Box!

Amanita: Let me give you a quick how-to!{VAR BE01}
If there's a Pokémon you often use in
your battles, you can register it in the{VAR BE00}
Battle Box!

Amanita: Please do use the Battle Box.{VAR BE01}
You can register Pokémon in the PC
over there, too!

Amanita: Oh, Trainer! Thank you very
much for helping Fennel!{VAR BE01}
This is from me. Please take it.
Don't be shy.{VAR BE01}

You can register your friends in your
Pal Pad.{VAR BE01}
After you register, you can link with
those friends over Nintendo Wi-Fi{VAR BE00}
Connection to do all kinds of fun things!{VAR BE01}
You can trade Pokémon, challenge
your friends to a battle, and so on.{VAR BE01}
Let me give you a quick how-to on
registering your friends.{VAR BE01}
You can either input your friend's code
directly by using your Pal Pad...{VAR BE01}
Or you can use the IR Connection
feature of the C-Gear.{VAR BE01}
Then, you can register your friend!{VAR BE01}

In the Battle Box, you can register up
to six Pokémon that you often use{VAR BE00}
in battles.{VAR BE01}
When you battle using Infrared
Connection, you can choose to battle{VAR BE00}
with either your party Pokémon or with{VAR BE00}
the Pokémon in the Battle Box!

